          "file": "basalt/auto/Auto.java",
          "line": 40,
          "javadoc": "Picks a model for you.\n\n<p>This is the one-call tier: hand it features and targets and it decides whether the problem is\nclassification or regression, screens every registered algorithm of that task with\ncross-validation, refits the winner on all rows, and reports how it did on a held-out slice.</p>\n\n<pre>{@code\nAutoModel model = Auto.quickstart(features, labels);\ndouble[] prediction = model.predict(unseen);\nSystem.out.println(model.summary());\n}</pre>\n\n<p>Anything you might want to control is on {@link Builder}: the seed, the number of folds, the\nheld-out fraction, the metric, and which candidates take part. Candidates come from\n{@link Registry}, so an algorithm registered by your own code is screened alongside the built-ins\nwithout any change here.</p>\n\n<p>The task is inferred from the targets: every value must be finite, and if all of them are\nwhole numbers with at most {@value #MAX_CLASSES} distinct values, the run is treated as\nclassification. Pass {@code task(...)} when the inference is wrong — a regression target that\nhappens to be integral, for example.</p>",
          "nested": [
            "Builder"
          ],
          "members": [
            {
              "kind": "field",
              "key": "MAX_CLASSES",
              "signature": "int MAX_CLASSES = 20",
              "params": [],
              "throws": [],
              "javadoc": "",
              "doc": {
                "summary": "判定为分类时允许的最大类别数",
                "body": [
                  "默认 20。同时受样本量约束：上限取 MAX_CLASSES 与 样本数/5 的较小者，避免小样本上把回归目标误判成分类。"
                ]
              }
            },
